---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Write a Pact file from a collection's http requests and their assertions

Usage: rustman contract pact generate [OPTIONS] --consumer <NAME> --provider <NAME> [COLLECTION]...

Arguments:
  [COLLECTION]...
          Collection folders or request files (default: the whole workspace)

Options:
      --consumer <NAME>
          The consumer's name

      --provider <NAME>
          The provider's name

      --pact-version <VERSION>
          The Pact Specification version to write
          
          [default: 4]
          [possible values: 3, 4]

      --output <FILE>
          The file to write (default: contracts/pacts/<consumer>-<provider>.json in the workspace)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
